I think he may have missed the point of the particular passage he quoted,
which had to do with the effect of legalizing the adoption market. I
thought I made it clear that I was talking about the production of children
to be adopted by infertile couples. In that situation, the adoptive
parents, who are the ones raising the kid, presumably are married.

For far as the nature vs nurture issue on personality, my evidence is
anecdotal. My elder son was reared almost entirely by his mother until he
became old enough to spend summers with me, since we separated shortly
after he was born. In personality he is strikingly similar to both me and
my father, and very unlike either his mother or step father. My (current)
wife  says that watching the three of us in one room is almost like
watching the same person at three different ages.

